% PowerPoint slide 1.
# CSE450 Translation of Programming Languages
## Lecture 9 : Live Coding
---
### Expression Grammar
...
From Class:
```
expr -> NUM 'd' NUM
      | expr '+' expr
      | expr '-' expr
      | MIN'('expr, expr')'
      | MAX'('expr, expr')'
      | '(' expr ')'
      | NUM
      | ID
```
...
@(700, 230) Issues:
...
@(700, 280) - '+' and '-' should be left associative.
...
@(700, 330) - we need to have precedence.
---
### Expression Grammar
Updated:
```
expr -> NUM 'd' NUM
      | expr '+' expr
      | expr '-' expr
term -> MIN'('expr, expr')'
      | MAX'('expr, expr')'
      | '(' expr ')'
      | NUM
      | ID
```
---
### Expression Grammar
Updated:
```
expr -> NUM 'd' NUM
      | expr '+' term
      | expr '-' term
term -> MIN'('expr, expr')'
      | MAX'('expr, expr')'
      | '(' expr ')'
      | NUM
      | ID
```
---
### Expression Grammar
Updated:
```
expr -> expr '+' expr2
      | expr '-' expr2
expr2 -> term 'd' term
      | term
term -> MIN'('expr, expr')'
      | MAX'('expr, expr')'
      | '(' expr ')'
      | NUM
      | ID
```
